# RUNTIME SPEND STATE, NOT SOURCE. Both were tracked and should not have been.
#
# .spend-by-day.json is this machine's daily spend total. Committing it means
# every clone inherits one operator's local ledger -- and this one carried a
# fabricated $117.53 for 2026-08-26, written when the test suite was still
# pointing at the operator's real file. With a daily ceiling configured, that
# phantom figure refuses real runs against money nobody spent.
#
# .lock is a zero-byte fcntl artifact. A committed lock file is a stale lock
# file in every checkout.
.spend-by-day.json
.spend-by-day.json.lock
